      "adviceAction": "Encash",
      "adviceActionRationale": [
        {
          "text": "I would recommend you withdraw the full amount of this pension under the small pots rules and put the money into your savings account. This would not detract from your financial retirement plan. Under the small pot rules, a \u00A3200 pension fund withdrawal would be taxed with 25% taken as tax-free cash and the remaining 75% taxed as income at your marginal tax rate. We estimate you would receive \u00A3170 net. If you were to leave this pot to grow until you retire, you could potentially take the full amount within your personal allowance, meaning no tax would be due.",
          "topic": "SmallPotsEncashment",
          "isClientSpecific": true,
          "provenance": {
